  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "read-me-screens",
      "page": "screens",
      "x": -420,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 340,
      "text": "DIRECTION A - NEON RAIN  (chosen)\n\nDeep blue-black, cyan + magenta, glass panels, scanlines and grain.\n\nTen screens now. Placeholders still to replace:\n- 'NOCTURNE' is a stand-in app name\n- posters are abstract art, not real key art\n- all counts, scores and match % are sample data\n\nOn the Home artboard the chips above the frame change the accent colour and toggle the scanlines."
    },
    {
      "id": "read-me-directions",
      "page": "directions",
      "x": -420,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 340,
      "text": "NOT TAKEN\n\nThe two alternates we passed on, kept for reference.\n\nB - ARCHIVE TERMINAL: amber on warm black, films as a ledger.\n\nC - HAZARD HUD: hazard yellow, clipped corners, glitched title."
    },
    {
      "id": "read-me-naming",
      "page": "naming",
      "x": -420,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 340,
      "text": "NAMING\n\nFour candidates in the Neon Rain wordmark treatment, each with how it looks in the nav rail.\n\nNOCTURNE is the incumbent. LATENT and HALIDE are the two I would push for - both are drawn from photographic chemistry, so they say 'film' without saying 'movies'.\n\nNothing here has been checked for trademark or domain availability."
    }
  ],
